#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:5
#: 54ac461bc532405ca5e360d02648f37c
msgid "Intel Aero RTF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:10
#: 0c31729d61304bf99e6156e296ede21f
msgid "The `Intel Aero RTF vehicle <https://software.intel.com/en-us/aero/drone-kit>`__ includes the :ref:`Intel Aero compute board <common-intel-aero-overview>`, `Vision Accessory Kit <https://software.intel.com/en-us/aero/vision-kit>`__ and a `Spektrum DXe transmitter <http://spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdId=SPM1000>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:13
#: 4cc7603f077641fb9ad2a27bb20bf251
msgid "Within the vehicle is an STM32F427V autopilot board which can run ArduPilot (replacing the pre-loaded non-ArduPilot software). In this way, the higher powered :ref:`Intel Aero compute board <common-intel-aero-overview>` is used as a `companion computer <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/companion-computers.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:20
#: 8492e589e09c483bb0e54911d5fa474a
msgid "Additional parts to buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:22
#: 1430c85cd90349b5ae81c711d7d7fa81
msgid "Although \"Ready-to-fly\" some additional parts are required to complete the upgrade and fly with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:24
#: 5a00d7490ce444ff8bb64813bda65eef
msgid "LiPo battery `3S <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/multistar-high-capacity-3s-5200mah-multi-rotor-lipo-pack.html?___store=en_us>`__ or `4S <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/multistar-high-capacity-5200mah-4s-12c-multi-rotor-lipo-pack-w-xt60.html?___store=en_us>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:25
#: 84d4ad1c1ff24010acc0424de2566a1d
msgid "2GB (or larger) USB thumb drive (`like this one <https://www.amazon.com/SanDisk-Cruzer-Glide-Drive-SDCZ60-008G-B35/dp/B007YX9O94/ref=sr_1_4?ie=UTF8&qid=1492397331&sr=8-4>`__) is needed for updating to the last release of the Linux distro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:26
#: e637828fda404f639e5c4a3ae668d5ff
msgid "Micro USB OTG to USB cable (`like this one <https://www.amazon.com/Micro-USB-OTG-Go-Adapter/dp/B005GI2VMG>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:27
#: 78ee87d6cceb422797355e0d292599a4
msgid "`Spektrum USB programming cable <https://www.spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdID=SPMA3065>`__ (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:30
#: 5f9c3e0a02b34d3c88edf84dacb8532a
msgid "Upgrading the vehicle's software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:32
#: 0b6828f377664a9a85a32d7b5209ea76
msgid "The Aero RTF may not have the last BIOS and Linux operating system. The Linux distro on Aero needs to be updated to version 1.2 in order for the autopilot to be flashed with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:35
#: d4f728943dd74220ae92bfb887b60ac9
msgid "`Official Setup Instructions from Intel <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup>`__ should be followed which will ask you to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:37
#: ee1939c58e4843a38bef29fffef872f3
msgid "Download the latest OS image (aka \"intel-aero-image-intel-aero.iso\") and Capsule/BIOS (aka \"capsule-01.00.12-r0.core2_64.rpm\") from the `Intel Download Center <https://downloadcenter.intel.com/download/26500/UAV-installation-files-for-Intel-Aero-Platform>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:38
#: 42adcb2113124c6c943cce8a124b6d58
msgid "`Flash the BIOS to Aero compute board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-bios>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:39
#: 71d52d628f034546815ce3c389b4e33e
msgid "`Flash the OS image to the Aero compute board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flash-intel-aero-linux-distribution>`__ using a USB thumb drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:40
#: ec7ef49b12014d7cac1704f5c77a7772
msgid "`Upgrade the FPGA <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-fpga>`__ using a .jam file included on the OS image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:42
#: 3926a7429cde43368b328f6c53d09211
msgid "The final step is to copy the **arducopter.px4** firmware to the Aero compute board and then flash it to the flight board:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:44
#: 13196019c9bd48aeac446f0ef2392274
msgid "Download the latest aero-fc ArduPilot firmware from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Copter/latest/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:45
#: 519cf6e7f6284216a92d2fe56d733dc0
msgid "Copy the above firmware to the Aero compute board in much the same way the BIOS's .rpm file was copied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:46
#: c87c6ef315ea4e9eaeb583ad2e1129dc
msgid "`Flash the autopilot board <https://github.com/intel-aero/meta-intel-aero/wiki/02-Initial-setup#flashing-the-flight-controller-rtf-only>`__ with the **ardupilot.px4** firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:48
#: b1b570c29b4a4a08b07ed835be4468d5
msgid "If you are developing ArduPilot, you can flash directly from the command line after compiling. Refer to `Build instructions <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/BUILD.md>`__ for more detailed instructions, but it's basically the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-intel-aero-rtf.rst:50
#: 077e8ffd84f4467392faa5af2aa765fa
msgid "./waf configure --board aerofc-v1 ./waf copter --upload"
msgstr ""

